schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Local Node (regen network chapter)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A small, place-based chapter of a wider regenerative network that runs its
    own projects and coordination — the article's central unit of analysis for
    where founding pitfalls occur.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used throughout common-pitfalls.md as the thing being founded/stewarded;
    contrasted against "the wider network" (e.g. Greenpill Network, Regen
    Coordination Hub) it connects to without being absorbed by.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - chapter (Greenpill's term for the same unit)
    - DAO (a local node may or may not formalize as one)
  important_distinctions:
    - "a local node is autonomous-yet-connected, distinct from both full isolation and full absorption into a parent network"
  tensions:
    - autonomy vs shared-learning
    - technology-first vs relationships-first founding
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating "local node" as synonymous with "DAO" erases that most founding
    failures in the article are social/organizational, not technical.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/common-pitfalls.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-143cd63d37c3
  source_lineage: common-pitfalls.md
